    "388": {
      "date": "2026-10-15",
      "edition": "Thursday 15 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Lions Women",
          "heading": "Jo Yapp's Lions Women face France in historic first Test in Cardiff",
          "body": "The British and Irish Lions Women will play their first-ever Test against France at Cardiff's Principality Stadium, ahead of their inaugural tour of New Zealand, where they face the Black Ferns. Head coach Jo Yapp said: \"There are moments in sport that only come around once and this is one of them.\" France have finished second behind the Red Roses in each of the past seven Six Nations and reached the 2025 World Cup semi-final, so the Lions have picked a stern opener."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Fiji hire Jake White as head coach after Mick Byrne's removal",
