      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Next generation",
          "heading": "Rory McHaffie, Jamie Stewart and Callum Reidy make Edinburgh and Glasgow debuts",
          "body": "Three of Scotland's next generation have made their first appearances for Edinburgh and Glasgow in the United Rugby Championship this season. Rory McHaffie, the Scotland Under-20s winger, came off the bench against Ulster in Belfast before scoring the winning try on his home debut at the Hive against Stormers. Prop Jamie Stewart made his Edinburgh debut in Italy against Zebre Parma, replacing Pierre Schoeman in the 73rd minute, while scrum-half Callum Reidy, Scottish-qualified, debuted in Glasgow's 36-19 win over Connacht. Both clubs remain undefeated in the competition."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Fiji hire Jake White as head coach after Mick Byrne's removal",
