        {
          "kicker": "Kit jibe",
          "heading": "Argentina wore 1986 World Cup football kit replica against England in Santiago",
          "body": "Argentina wore a one-off darker blue Le Coq Sportif retro kit with silver numbers in their Round three Nations Championship match against England in Santiago del Estero, copying the strip Diego Maradona wore for the football team at the 1986 World Cup, The Sun reported. The Pumas lost 24-31 that day, and Argentina's own post read: \"Memories that span generations and remain alive in the collective memory.\" The stunt drew heavy attention on social media."
        },
